"""
ai_detector.py
--------------
AI Content Detection Engine for the Resume Screening System.

VERSION 3.0 â€” HYBRID ML + HEURISTIC ARCHITECTURE
â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•

Replaces the v2 heuristic-only system with a data-driven approach:

    70%  â€”  ML Model (Logistic Regression on 12 statistical features)
    30%  â€”  Simplified Heuristic Signals (3 statistical signals, no keyword lists)

WHY ML IS BETTER THAN PURE HEURISTICS:
    Heuristic v2 matched specific keywords ("proven track record", "spearheaded")
    which triggered false positives on well-written human resumes that naturally
    use professional language. The ML model instead learns the statistical
    fingerprint of AI text â€” uniform sentence lengths, low entropy, predictable
    word distributions â€” which generalizes far better.

CLASSIFICATION (v3.1 â€” lowered thresholds to reduce false positives):
    0â€“40   â†’ "Likely Human"
    40â€“70  â†’ "Uncertain"
    70â€“100 â†’ "Likely AI"

SECTION FILTERING:
    Skills sections, bullet-point lists, and headers are EXCLUDED from
    per-sentence analysis. Only paragraph-based content (summaries,
    experience descriptions) is scored.

GRACEFUL DEGRADATION:
    If the trained model file is not found, falls back to heuristic-only mode.
    Run `python train_model.py` to generate the model.

BACKWARD COMPATIBILITY:
    - detect_ai_content(text) â†’ Tuple[float, dict]  (unchanged)
    - detect_ai_sections(text) â†’ list                (unchanged)
    - Response dict format is compatible with api.py, app.py, main.py
"""

